  "notes": "Motorola SWTV-24AE-FHD (Skyworth OEM, device beomil, product SW11_TG, MediaTek), India/Global\nAndroid TV 14 (API 34), build UKN4.250714.138, security patch 2025-10-01.\nStock launcher: com.google.android.apps.tv.launcherx (Google TV).\nSetup wizard: com.google.android.tungsten.setupwraith (claims HOME with priority 1).\nLive TV app: com.cltv.hybrid (iWedia CanaliTV).\nHDMI and tuner inputs: com.mediatek.tvinput.\nRemote: Settings button emits keycode 83 (KEYCODE_NOTIFICATION) on scancode 240; needs HomeKeyService.\n\nApply:   TV_HOST=<tv ip> tools/disable.sh examples/motorola-swtv-24ae-fhd/debloat.txt\nUndo:    TV_HOST=<tv ip> tools/restore.sh examples/motorola-swtv-24ae-fhd/debloat.txt com.google.android.apps.tv.launcherx\nEverything is DISABLED, not uninstalled. Comment out any line you want to keep.\n\nWARNING: If Wi-Fi was set up during the first-run wizard, the saved network belongs to setupwraith\nand Android DELETES it the moment setupwraith is disabled; the TV drops off the network and ADB with it.\nCheck first: `dumpsys wifi | grep -o 'cname=[^ ]*'`. If it is not android.uid.system, forget the network\nand re-join it in Settings > Network BEFORE disabling setupwraith.\nSkyworth telemetry and activation",
